  f('C.5','Small Doppler shift for light',t`\frac{\Delta f}{f}=\frac{\Delta\lambda}{\lambda}\approx\frac{v}{c}`,'The booklet writes the fractional shift magnitudes as equal in the low-speed approximation v ≪ c. For recession wavelength increases while frequency decreases; their signed fractional changes have opposite signs. Outside this approximation, the two fractional magnitudes are not exactly equal.', t`\Delta f|magnitude of frequency change|Hz;f|emitted frequency|Hz;\Delta\lambda|magnitude of wavelength change|m;\lambda|emitted wavelength|m;v|radial relative speed|m s⁻¹;c|speed of light|m s⁻¹`,10);
